ַטּוֺחָם Exod 7:12 ; Numbers 17:21; also מַטָּיו Hab 3:14 (but read מַטֶּיךָ or — Gr — מַטֹּתֶיךָ ); — 1 (compare שֵׁבֶט מַקֵּל, ) staff of traveller Gen 38:18 , 25 (J); in General Isa 10:15 (simile; || שֵׁבֶט ); from staff as support comes figurative מַטֵּהלֶֿחֶם staff of bread (food supply) Ezek 4:16 ; 5:16 ; 14:13 ; Lev 26:26 ; Psa 105:16 ; of staff or rod, Moses as shepherd Exod 4:2 , 4 ; 7:15 (J), 4:17 ; 7:17 , 20 ; 9:23 ; 10:13 ; 17:5 (all E); compare also Isa 10:26 ; Exod 14:16 ; Num 20:8-9 , 11 (all P); called ׳מ הָאֱלֹהִים Exod 4:20 ; 17:9 (both E), because of miraculous power connected with it; compare mirac. rod of Aaron 7:9-10 , 12 , 19 ; 8:1 ; 8:12 ; 8:13 (all P), and of Egyptian magicians 7:12 (twice in verse) (P); compare Aaron's rod that budded Numbers 17:18; Numbers 17:21; Numbers 17:23; Numbers 17:25 (compare RS Semitic i. 180; 2d ed. 197 ); carried even by warrior 1Sam 14:27 , 43 ; שִׁכְמוֺ מַטֵּה Isa 9:3 i.e. rod that strikes his shoulder, task-master's rod (|| בּוֺ הַנֹּגֵשׂ שֵׁבֶט ), compare 10:5 and 10:24 ; 14:5 (|| שֵׁבֶט ), all figurative of oppression; מוּסָדָה מַטֵּה 30:32 appointed rod (of punishment); compare ׳מ Ezek 7:10-11 , (but text obscure, Co — q. v. &#8212; sceptre) , also Micah 6:9 according to ᵑ0 , but see below 3 ; used in beating out ( חבט ) fennel Isa 28:27 ; staff as badge of leader or ruler מַטֵּהעֹֿז Jer 48:17 (|| מַקֵּל ), compare Psa 110:2 ; so Numbers 17:17 (4 t. in verse) + 10 t. Numbers 17; apparently shafts , i.e. arrows or spears, Hab 3:9 , 14 (compare Now Da GASm). 2 branch of vine Ezek 19:11-12 , 14 (twice in verse). 3 tribe (183 t.), originally company led by chief with staff: specifically of tribes of Israel in both singular and plural, 1Kin 7:14 ; 8:1 2Chr 5:2 ; Exod 31:2 5 t. Exodus; Lev 24:11 ; Num 1:4 89t. Numbers; Josh 7:1 56t. Joshua (all P); 1Chr 6:45 21 t. 1 Chronicles 6; 12:31 ; probably also Micah 6:9 (vocative; so ᵐ5 We Now GASm). — compare שֵׁבֶט , and on relation of these two words for tribe Hebrew usage D